{"id":"s7","level":5,"levelName":"Structure and style","n":3,"of":14,"title":"Saying when","titleHe":"פִּסְקַת זְמַן","goal":"Attach a clause of time — before, after, while, until, ever since.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Almost every word for when in Hebrew is a preposition with שֶׁ stuck on the end. The preposition takes a noun; add שֶׁ and it takes a whole clause instead. That one rule generates the entire table below."},{"type":"table","caption":"Before a noun, and before a clause","head":["meaning","with a noun","with a clause"],"rows":[["before","לִפְנֵי הָאֲרוּחָה","לִפְנֵי שֶׁאָכַלְנוּ"],["after","אַחֲרֵי הַשִּׁעוּר","אַחֲרֵי שֶׁגָּמַרְנוּ"],["until","עַד הָעֶרֶב","עַד שֶׁהוּא בָּא"],["since","מֵאָז הַבֹּקֶר","מֵאָז שֶׁהוּא הָלַךְ"],["during, while","בִּזְמַן הָעֲבוֹדָה","בִּזְמַן שֶׁעָבַדְתִּי"]]},{"type":"text","body":"Two more do not follow the pattern and have to be learned as they are: כְּשֶׁ, when, which only ever takes a clause; and כָּל עוֹד, as long as, which takes one without any שֶׁ at all."},{"type":"table","caption":"The rest of the set","head":["meaning","Hebrew"],"rows":[["when","כְּשֶׁ־"],["when — in writing","כַּאֲשֶׁר"],["the moment that","בָּרֶגַע שֶׁ־"],["every time that","כָּל פַּעַם שֶׁ־"],["as long as","כָּל עוֹד"],["while, in the time that","בְּעוֹד"]]},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"כְּשֶׁהָיִיתִי יֶלֶד גַּרְנוּ בַּכְּפָר.","en":"When I was a child we lived in the village."},{"he":"חִכִּיתִי עַד שֶׁהִיא חָזְרָה.","en":"I waited until she came back."},{"he":"לִפְנֵי שֶׁתֵּלֵךְ, תֵּן לִי דַּקָּה.","en":"Before you go, give me a minute."},{"he":"כָּל עוֹד יֵשׁ זְמַן, אֶפְשָׁר לְחַכּוֹת.","en":"As long as there's time, one can wait."}]},{"type":"tip","body":"לִפְנֵי שֶׁ and אַחֲרֵי שֶׁ take a tensed verb, not an infinitive. English says before going; Hebrew says before that I went — לִפְנֵי שֶׁהָלַכְתִּי — and the tense follows the main clause."}],"vocab":[{"he":"כְּשֶׁ","en":"when","translit":"kshe"},{"he":"לִפְנֵי שֶׁ","en":"before (a clause)","translit":"lifnei she"},{"he":"אַחֲרֵי שֶׁ","en":"after (a clause)","translit":"acharei she"},{"he":"עַד שֶׁ","en":"until","translit":"ad she"},{"he":"מֵאָז שֶׁ","en":"ever since","translit":"me'az she"},{"he":"בִּזְמַן שֶׁ","en":"while","translit":"bizman she"},{"he":"כָּל עוֹד","en":"as long as","translit":"kol od"},{"he":"בָּרֶגַע שֶׁ","en":"the moment that","translit":"barega she"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["a little, few","man","when","lest"],"correct":2,"prompt":"כְּשֶׁ","translit":"kshe"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["bank","before (a clause)","day","all the more so"],"correct":1,"prompt":"לִפְנֵי שֶׁ","translit":"lifnei she"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["on the one hand","after (a clause)","travels, rides","camera"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אַחֲרֵי שֶׁ","translit":"acharei she"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["his house","to her","until","fear"],"correct":2,"prompt":"עַד שֶׁ","translit":"ad she"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["like, as","ever since","arranged, tidy","bathroom, bath"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מֵאָז שֶׁ","translit":"me'az she"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["to say (Aramaic)","nine (f.)","children","while"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בִּזְמַן שֶׁ","translit":"bizman she"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["autumn","as long as","rich","when (literary)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"כָּל עוֹד","translit":"kol od"},{"type":"choice","q":"The rest of the set — when?","options":["בָּרֶגַע שֶׁ־","כַּאֲשֶׁר","כָּל פַּעַם שֶׁ־","כְּשֶׁ־"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"The rest of the set — every time that?","options":["כְּשֶׁ־","כַּאֲשֶׁר","בָּרֶגַע שֶׁ־","כָּל פַּעַם שֶׁ־"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"כָּל עוֹד יֵשׁ זְמַן, אֶפְשָׁר ___.","en":"As long as there's time, one can wait.","options":["לִפְנֵי שֶׁ","לְחַכּוֹת","כָּל עוֹד","בִּזְמַן שֶׁ"],"correct":1,"full":"כָּל עוֹד יֵשׁ זְמַן, אֶפְשָׁר לְחַכּוֹת."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “after (a clause)”?","options":["חָתוּל","מַבְטִיחַ","אַחֲרֵי שֶׁ","מַמְלָכָה"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"The rest of the set — while, in the time that?","options":["בָּרֶגַע שֶׁ־","בְּעוֹד","כַּאֲשֶׁר","כְּשֶׁ־"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["כְּשֶׁ","when"],["לִפְנֵי שֶׁ","before (a clause)"],["אַחֲרֵי שֶׁ","after (a clause)"],["עַד שֶׁ","until"],["מֵאָז שֶׁ","ever since"]]},{"type":"build","tokens":["עַד","שֶׁהִיא","חָזְרָה","חִכִּיתִי"],"answer":["חִכִּיתִי","עַד","שֶׁהִיא","חָזְרָה"],"en":"I waited until she came back."},{"type":"build","tokens":["לִי","תֵּן","שֶׁתֵּלֵךְ,","לִפְנֵי","דַּקָּה"],"answer":["לִפְנֵי","שֶׁתֵּלֵךְ,","תֵּן","לִי","דַּקָּה"],"en":"Before you go, give me a minute."},{"type":"type","q":"Write “as long as” in Hebrew","answer":"כָּל עוֹד","hint":"kol od"}]}